      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like one additional place may need to be updated as part of this change. \n\nThe corresponding property in `java/com/google/gerrit/pgm/init/InitLogging.java` does not appear to have been adjusted yet.\n\nAs a result, a newly initialized Gerrit site still ends up with a `gerrit.config` that references the Log4j Flogger (1.x) backend rather than the Log4j2 Flogger backend, which leads to a broken configuration for fresh installs.\n\nThis also raises the question of how existing Gerrit sites should be migrated once this change is merged. It might be helpful to mention in the commit message that the `init` program needs to be re-run, or alternatively that the `-Dflogger.backend_factory` Java system property must be updated manually. For example:\n\n```ini\n[container]\n\tjavaOptions \u003d \"-Dflogger.backend_factory\u003dcom.google.common.flogger.backend.log4j2.Log4j2BackendFactory#getInstance\"\n```",
