      "writtenOn": "2026-01-08T23:22:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like the SLF4J bridge artifact name is slightly off here — the correct one is `log4j-slf4j2-impl` (with `slf4j2`, not `slf4j`).\n\nWith the Log4j 2 version currently in use, the dependency would be:\n\n```python\nmaven_jar(\n    name \u003d \"impl-log4j\",\n    artifact \u003d \"org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-slf4j2-impl:\" + LOG4J2_VERS,\n    sha1 \u003d \"a5ed4c3e2effa2575a4dde13f9101bfe23ccfb1a\",\n)\n```\n\nWhen using the older `log4j-slf4j-impl` artifact together with newer SLF4J APIs, the mismatch is usually visible at runtime. For example, starting Gerrit with additional Log4j2 debug flags from the command line:\n\n```bash\n$\u003e java -Dorg.apache.logging.log4j.level\u003dDEBUG \\\n   -Dlog4j2.debug\u003dtrue \\ \n   -Dflogger.backend_factory\u003d... \\\n   -Dflogger.logging_context\u003d... \\  \n   -jar /Users/Davido/projects/test_site/bin/gerrit.war \\\n   daemon \\\n   -d /Users/Davido/projects/test_site\n```\n\ntypically results in warnings like:\n\n[...]\n```bash\nSLF4J(W): No SLF4J providers were found.\nSLF4J(W): Defaulting to no-operation (NOP) logger implementation\nSLF4J(W): See https://www.slf4j.org/codes.html#noProviders for further details.\nSLF4J(W): Class path contains SLF4J bindings targeting slf4j-api versions 1.7.x or earlier.\nSLF4J(W): Ignoring binding found at [jar:file:/Users/Davido/.gerritcodereview/tmp/gerrit_710595449436894837_app/log4j-slf4j-impl-2.25.1.jar!/org/slf4j/impl/StaticLoggerBinder.class]\nSLF4J(W): See https://www.slf4j.org/codes.html#ignoredBindings for an explanation.\n[...]\n```\n\nUsing log4j-slf4j2-impl avoids this mismatch and ensures the SLF4J bridge matches the Log4j 2 / SLF4J 2 setup.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 113,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 113,
        "endChar": 61
